OL,3,AInterest rates held but Bank signals
OL,4,Arise if energy prices stay high
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Bank of England has held interest
OL,7,Frates at their current rate of 3.75%
OL,8,Ffor the sixth time in a row but said
OL,9,Fthey were likely to rise if high energy
OL,10,Fprices persist.
OL,12,FThe US-Israel war with Iran has
OL,13,Fdisrupted global energy supplies
OL,14,Fleading to a sharp increase in petrol
OL,15,Fand diesel prices and an uptick in
OL,16,Finflation.
OL,18,FBut Bank of England governor Andrew
OL,19,FBailey said energy price volatility
OL,20,Fmade it more likely that interest rates
OL,21,Fwould rise.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,311,300,200,140,0,100
